  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The first step is anti addition of <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> across the double bond.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0112_2978edb09aa7.png\" style=\"width: 372px; height: 115px;\" /><br /><br />In the second step, <math><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> <math><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> ) gets added by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math> mechanism. And <math><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> from the dashed position acts as the leaving group leads to the formation of a stable benzylic carbocation.<br /><br /><img height=\"107\" src=\"assets\\st0112_a5bf0cfb39c4.png\" width=\"349\" /></p>"
